import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy" lede="No analytics, no cookies, no accounts, no tracking.">
  <p>
    This site is a set of static files. It does not set cookies, run analytics, or record what you
    search for.
  </p>
  <h2>Who else your browser talks to</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>OpenFreeMap</strong> serves the basemap tiles on the map page. Like any web server it
      sees your IP address when your browser asks for tiles.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our Native Land Digital relay</strong> (on Vercel), when you look up a place or follow
      a nation on the map. It receives a point, rounded to about a kilometer, and stores nothing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Where you live</strong>, only if you look up a place. The address you type goes
      through our relay to the US Census Bureau’s geocoder (or, if Census finds no match,
      OpenStreetMap’s Nominatim) and comes back as coordinates rounded to about 100 meters. Nothing
      is stored. The address stays in the part of the web address after the #, which browsers do not
      send to servers; after the lookup it is replaced by the rounded coordinates, so a link you
      share points to a neighborhood, not a house. Everything else about the place is worked out in
      your browser. “Use my location” asks your browser and sends your location nowhere except the
      territory lookup below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our private intake</strong> (on Vercel), only if you send the claim or correction
      form. What you write goes to a private inbox and is never published.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Fonts and everything else are served from this site. The search runs entirely in your browser.
  </p>
</Page>
